From 577af0e6ef92a00d7a253ec7d555da8e0f276501 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Seamans <seamansgraham@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:07:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add transfer-impedance layers on FEM-BEM interfaces

A thin resistive/inertive sheet across an opening (felt, acoustic cloth)
is two-sided, so it is a property of the interface, not an impedance wall.
boundary.parameters["transfer_impedance"] = {"model": "resistance_mass",
"resistance_pa_s_per_m": R, "mass_kg_per_m2": M} on the interface's
bounded (FEM-side) boundary makes BEAT Engine 0.3.0+ti1 enforce
p_FEM - p_BEM = (R + i omega M) v_n.

- acoustic_materials: strict parser (all keys required, R, M finite >= 0).
- physical_compiler: only on interface boundaries in bounded air; assumption.
- coupled_backend: accept the key on the bounded interface side; refuse it
  on the one-shot stdin path, which cannot negotiate the worker's
  interface_transfer_impedance capability (the persistent worker does, via
  negotiate_submission); fail any result whose diagnostics do not echo the
  requested layers.
- System dialog: show the layer on interface rows and keep it on save,
  instead of silently dropping it; it does not edit it.
- Tests and docs (Physical System Model, Coupled Solver, Phasor Convention).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MXLCRc7E1cDCAXXCEn1VoL
